// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5957 new: Browser Extension Force Install via Policy Detection (Windows, macOS, Linux)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5957
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Suspicious Browser Extension Force Install via Policy on Linux
// Sigma ID: 131e1902-093b-4eb7-99f7-17c6e86dfcf5
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001
// Description: Detects the creation or modification of browser policy JSON files on Linux that can force-
//   install extensions. The ExtensionInstallForcelist and ExtensionSettings policies silently
//   install extensions that users cannot disable or remove. Adversaries may abuse these to persist
//   malicious browser extensions without user interaction.
// False positives:
//   - Enterprise IT administrators deploying browser extensions via policy files
//   - Package managers installing browser policy packages
// References:
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionInstallForcelist
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionSettings
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-policies#extensioninstallforcelist
//   - https://support.google.com/chrome/a/answer/9027408
//   - https://github.com/praetorian-inc/ChromeAlone
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/526405083b950916d7e784ee66c6fab0b0211c44/rules/linux/file_event/file_event_lnx_browser_extension_force_install_policy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "/etc/opt/chrome/policies/managed/" or FolderPath contains "/etc/opt/chrome/policies/recommended/") or (FolderPath contains "/etc/chromium/policies/managed/" or FolderPath contains "/etc/chromium/policies/recommended/") or FolderPath contains "/etc/opt/edge/policies/managed/"
